 ## Get started
 
+### CLI
+
+Preview rows as JSON, run SQL to filter, group, or join tables, and save results
+as Arrow or JSON. Queries run locally.
+
+With [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/) installed,
+run the CLI from PyPI without adding it to your project:
+
+```bash
+uvx --no-build delta-arrow-reader@latest preview /path/to/delta-table --column id --limit 3
+```
+
+Replace the path with a Delta table directory and `id` with a column name.
+This prints up to three values as JSON, including the column's type.
+Continue with the [CLI quickstart](https://mag1cfrog.github.io/delta-arrow-reader/cli-quickstart/)
+or [SQL examples](https://mag1cfrog.github.io/delta-arrow-reader/cli-workflows/).
+See [installation](https://mag1cfrog.github.io/delta-arrow-reader/installation/#cli-binaries-and-container-images)
+for supported platforms, a persistent command, standalone `dar` binaries, and containers.
+
+For [Unity Catalog tables](https://mag1cfrog.github.io/delta-arrow-reader/unity-catalog/),
+reuse a working profile from the Databricks CLI installed on your `PATH`.
+Read tables by their `uc://catalog.schema.table` names and run SQL locally,
+without a Databricks cluster or SQL warehouse. The metastore must allow external
+data access, and your identity needs table read permissions plus `EXTERNAL USE SCHEMA`.
+The guide covers setup and supported tables.
+
