+## Try the command line
+
+Preview rows as JSON, run SQL to filter, group, or join tables, and save results
+as Arrow or JSON. With [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/)
+installed, run the CLI from PyPI without adding it to your project:
+
+```bash
+uvx --no-build delta-arrow-reader@latest preview /path/to/delta-table --column id --limit 3
+```
+
+Replace the path with a Delta table directory and `id` with a column name.
+This prints up to three values as JSON, including the column's type.
+Continue with the [CLI quickstart](cli-quickstart.md) or
+[SQL examples](cli-workflows.md). For supported platforms and other ways to
+install the command, see [installation](installation.md#cli-binaries-and-container-images).
+
+For [Unity Catalog tables](unity-catalog.md), reuse a working profile from the
+Databricks CLI installed on your `PATH`. Use `uc://catalog.schema.table` names;
+reads and SQL run locally. The metastore must allow external data access, and
+your identity needs table read permissions plus `EXTERNAL USE SCHEMA`.
+The guide covers setup and supported tables.
 
